# DNA-AND content · the grand tour: one flight from among the galaxies down to the quarks, for watching
# Run it: DNA-AND.exe --tour grand-tour   (any key or click takes the controls back). Edit the stops to make your own.
# Each @stop is done in order:
#   do: zoom    fly in (or out, with a negative rate) steadily until the view is "until-km" across (km, the distance to what
#               you look at); rate: tenfolds a second (one steady rate: each tenfold takes the same time), eased in and out
#               (a zoom that stops getting anywhere for six seconds goes on to the next stop)
#   do: orbit   circle slowly round what is picked (or look round if nothing is): turn degrees a second, for seconds
#   do: look    tilt your view up (+) or down (-) by tilt degrees over seconds, turning a little as it goes
#   do: pick    choose what to go to: galaxy, star, planet, none, atom, electron, nucleus, proton, quark
#   caption:    the words shown while the stop runs
# Sizes for scale: a galaxy about 1e18 km across, a star system about 1e10 km, Earth 12,742 km, a person 0.0018 km,
# a sand grain 2e-7 km, an atom 2e-13 km, a nucleus 1e-17 km, a proton 1.7e-18 km.

@stop leave
do: zoom
rate: -0.35
until-km: 3e20
caption: Leaving the galaxy behind: out among the galaxies

@stop galaxies
do: orbit
turn: 5
seconds: 22
caption: The universe: galaxies of every kind, each of a hundred billion stars

@stop choose-galaxy
do: pick
target: galaxy
caption: One galaxy

@stop round-galaxy
do: orbit
turn: 6
seconds: 14
caption: Its arms, its bulge, its clusters and nebulae

@stop into-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 1e16
caption: Into the galaxy, among its stars

@stop choose-star
do: pick
target: star
caption: A star

@stop into-system
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 2e9
caption: Down to the star and its planets

@stop round-system
do: orbit
turn: 7
seconds: 22
caption: Its solar system: the star, its planets and their moons, its belts

@stop choose-planet
do: pick
target: planet
caption: A world

@stop to-planet
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 4e4
caption: To the planet

@stop round-planet
do: orbit
turn: 8
seconds: 22
caption: The whole world: seas, land, clouds, air

@stop to-ground
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 0.002
caption: Down through the air to the ground

@stop stand
do: pick
target: none
caption: Standing on the ground, six feet up

@stop look-up
do: look
tilt: 55
turn: 6
seconds: 9
caption: Looking up into the sky and space

@stop sky
do: orbit
turn: 6
seconds: 12
caption: The sky, the star, the other worlds

@stop look-down
do: look
tilt: -95
turn: 4
seconds: 8
caption: And down to the ground at your feet

@stop to-grains
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 2e-6
caption: The ground breaks into stones, pebbles and grains of sand

@stop round-grains
do: orbit
turn: 8
seconds: 12
caption: Grains of the ground's own minerals, each its own shape

@stop to-face
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 2e-9
caption: Onto one grain: its steps, cracks, stains and the specks lying on it

@stop round-face
do: orbit
turn: 8
seconds: 10
caption: A grain's face: clay plates, iron skins, a film of water

@stop to-crystal
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 6e-12
caption: Its crystal: the atoms in their real places

@stop round-crystal
do: orbit
turn: 8
seconds: 14
caption: The lattice, every atom held by its shared electrons

@stop choose-atom
do: pick
target: atom
caption: One atom

@stop to-atom
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 6e-13
caption: Into one atom

@stop round-atom
do: orbit
turn: 9
seconds: 18
caption: An atom: its electrons in their shells round the nucleus, like a solar system; the outer (valence) shell in gold

@stop choose-electron
do: pick
target: electron
caption: Following one electron

@stop follow-electron
do: orbit
turn: 5
seconds: 14
caption: An electron, a point as far as anyone has measured, on its path round the nucleus

@stop choose-nucleus
do: pick
target: nucleus
caption: The nucleus

@stop to-nucleus
do: zoom
rate: 0.6
until-km: 3e-17
caption: Across the emptiness: the nucleus is a hundred thousand times smaller than the atom

@stop round-nucleus
do: orbit
turn: 8
seconds: 16
caption: The nucleus: its protons and neutrons, held by the strong force against the protons' electric push

@stop choose-proton
do: pick
target: proton
caption: One proton

@stop to-proton
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 2.5e-18
caption: Into a proton

@stop round-proton
do: orbit
turn: 8
seconds: 14
caption: A proton: three quarks, two up and one down, in the glow of the gluons

@stop choose-quark
do: pick
target: quark
caption: One quark

@stop to-quark
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 6e-19
caption: A quark and its colour charge

@stop end
do: orbit
turn: 5
seconds: 30
caption: The smallest things known: from here the universe is waves of its fields
